Use this command only from an active `itldev/*` development branch worktree.

Run the helper directly from the current project directory:

If the agent shell tool supports `timeout_ms`, run this lifecycle command with `timeout_ms >= 3900000` by default so the outer shell outlives the 3600-second Designer limit; if that limit is configured higher, raise the outer timeout too. Do not use `120000 ms` or other short defaults because the helper may launch 1C Designer/Enterprise operations.

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\.agents\skills\1c-workflow\scripts\run-itl-command.ps1 -- -Action refresh-dev-branch-lite
```

The helper never updates or reads the source infobase and never rebuilds the seed. It records the exact current `master` SHA, merges that commit while preserving branch `ConfigDumpInfo.xml`, re-executes updated workflow helpers when needed, performs the fingerprint-gated branch load and Enterprise normalization, and reconciles branch MCP configuration. This is the parallel-friendly second step after one `/itl-sync-master`.

On success with a non-empty `userReport`, normally make the final response exactly that report rendered as Markdown, with no introduction, conclusion, or separate success summary. If `requiredAction` begins with `classify-tests-after-refresh:`, continue in the same task: read `.agent-1c/verification-selection/inventory.json` and the suite-selection reference, classify the named Vanessa/YAxUnit tests and owners, split oversized or mixed feature files yourself while preserving scenario behavior, update the branch catalogs, and run the compact helper with `-Action validate-test-classification`; that action does not start 1C. Then report refresh plus classification. Do not ask the developer to classify or migrate tests. Outside that exception, do not translate, summarize, reorder, or omit report lines. On `errorCategory=merge-conflict` or `errorCategory=source-integrity`, use progressive semantic repair: begin with the conflicting semantic unit and preserve compatible deltas; widen to the object, callers, related source, history, tests, OpenSpec, and required product documentation only when a concrete uncertainty or failed check requires it. Stage the repair and repeat this same command. The helper records additional related 1C source as `repairPaths` and rejects unrelated paths. Ask the user only when evidence leaves incompatible business outcomes. Never create the merge commit manually. For any other failure, read only the last 80 lines of `logPath` when needed.
